# Ancient Cornucopia: "Whenever you cast a spell that's one or more colors, you may gain 1 life for each of that spell's colors.
# Do this only once each turn." (CR 603.2h: once Bot1 has gained life with it this turn it does not trigger again.)
# Turn 1: Bot1 casts Cornucopia, then a colorless Ornithopter: no trigger (the spell has no color; the refusal shows it is not asked).
# Turn 3: Lightning Helix is red and white, two colors: Bot1 accepts and gains 2 (and 3 from the Helix); then a Lightning Bolt, one
# color, is cast with Cornucopia's own mana and Bot1 is not asked at all (a refusal), because the life gain was done this turn.
# Turn 5: a new turn, so a Lightning Bolt (one color) triggers it again and Bot1 gains 1 (Cornucopia's mana pays for the Bolt).
# Life: 20 + 2 + 3 + 1 = 26; Bot2 takes 3 three times.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ancient Cornucopia
Lightning Helix
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

